--- TM14 red evidence appended by T3 (2026-11-02) ---
Repro: editor_boot on the t22 fixture, scene.bsn open, viewport 2D,
Ground layer + Tilemap tool + zoom 1.0, then input.pointer
press/move/release across world cells (8,72)->(88,72) — every point
inside the stage at zoom 1.
Observed: jackdaw/status modal stays "tilemap.stroke" after the release
(the app log above carries the run), zero TileGridCell rows appear.
Cause (source-level): tilemap_palette.rs stroke_cell() resolves
`hosts.get(state.stage?)` — the Viewport2dPanelHost component queried on
the captured STAGE entity — but the component lives on the panel content
entity the stage hangs from (viewport_2d.rs:1764 inserts it on `parent`,
`stage` is a separate child carrying Scene2dViewport). stroke_cell
therefore answers None every frame, and the None early-return precedes
the just_released check, so the modal never dispatches and never exits
until Esc/right-click (jackdaw/cancel clears it).
Headless blind spot: the T2 stage tests co-locate the host and the stage
on one entity, so the lookup succeeds there.
